<title>NORWAY: Algeria begins gas supplies to Italy's Enel-Statoil.</title>
<headline>Algeria begins gas supplies to Italy's Enel-Statoil.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deliveries of pipeline gas from Algeria's Sonatrach to Italian utility Enel started in October via the Transmed line from Tunis to Italy, Den norske stats oljeselskap AS said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Supplied from the Hassi R'Mel field under a 20-year contract, the gas will be piped to power stations in southern Italy by distributor SNAM SpA, a subsidiary of ENI SpA, Statoil's Status Weekly newsletter said.</p>
<p>SNAM will now transport 23 billion cubic metres per year of gas through the Transmed line, including four billion cubic metres for Enel at plateau, Statoil said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
